WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.640
Session security review starts with configuration and lifecycle.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:12.900
Inspect cookie attributes, session lifetime settings, token validation settings, logout behavior, renewal behavior, and framework defaults.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.920
Confirm that the application rotates or renews session state at important transitions such as login and privilege changes.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:26.700
Verify that password changes, account disablement, and permission changes have the intended effect on active sessions.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.240
These are design checks, code checks, and runtime behavior checks.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.100
Testing should include normal flows and edge cases.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.560
Confirm that logout prevents continued use of the old authenticated state.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.420
Verify idle and absolute timeouts.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.400
Inspect cookies with browser developer tools to confirm expected attributes, scope, and lifetime.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.460
Review API behavior for expired or invalid tokens.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.400
Confirm that sensitive actions still enforce server-side authorization and do not rely only on client-side state.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:04.620
Penetration testing observations should be translated into durable configuration or code fixes, not one-off patches.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.160
Logs and monitoring should be part of the review.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:13.300
Session events should support troubleshooting, security investigation, and operational monitoring without exposing secrets.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:24.560
Review whether session identifiers, access tokens, refresh tokens, or authorization headers can appear in logs, URLs, error reports, analytics, or support exports.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:34.540
Ask whether defenders can answer basic questions: who signed in, when sessions were created or ended, when privileges changed, and whether unusual session activity occurred.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.520
Testing is strongest when it proves both prevention and visibility.
